From: OpenGOAL ARM64 macOS port
Subject: [PATCH] Metal: invalidate context state when a flush ends the render encoder

BufferManager::getBuffer calls ContextMtl::flushCommandBuffer directly to
service an allocation, which can happen while a render pass is open. That
flush ends the render encoder, and RenderCommandEncoder::reset() clears
mPipelineStateSet while endEncodingImpl() resets mStateCache -- but unlike
getRenderPassCommandEncoder(), which explicitly does mDirtyBits.set() after
ending an encoder, this path leaves mDirtyBits untouched.

The next setupDraw() therefore sees DIRTY_BIT_RENDER_PIPELINE clear,
checkIfPipelineChanged() reports no change, and no setRenderPipelineState is
emitted onto the newly restarted encoder. The draw is then encoded with no
pipeline state bound, tripping

    ASSERT(mPipelineStateSet &&
           "Render Pipeline State was never set and we've issued a draw command.");

in debug builds. In release builds the ASSERT is compiled out and the draw
reaches Metal, which dereferences a null render-context pointer inside
-[AGXG16XFamilyRenderContext drawIndexedPrimitives:...].

Restore the same postcondition getRenderPassCommandEncoder documents, at the
point the encoder is actually destroyed. Gated on mRenderEncoder.valid() so
flushes with no live render encoder are unaffected.

Base revision: aa192212af54

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm
@@ void ContextMtl::flushCommandBuffer(mtl::CommandBufferFinishOperation operation)
 {
     mRenderPassesSinceFlush = 0;
     if (mCmdBuffer.ready())
     {
+        // Ending the render encoder resets its state (RenderCommandEncoder::reset
+        // clears mPipelineStateSet, and endEncodingImpl resets mStateCache), so any
+        // state we believe is already applied to it is gone. Callers that reach here
+        // from outside getRenderPassCommandEncoder (e.g. BufferManager::getBuffer
+        // flushing to service an allocation mid-render-pass) would otherwise leave
+        // mDirtyBits clear, and the next setupDraw would encode a draw with no
+        // render pipeline state bound.
+        const bool hadRenderEncoder = mRenderEncoder.valid();
         endEncoding(true);
+        if (hadRenderEncoder)
+        {
+            mDirtyBits.set();
+        }
         mCmdBuffer.commit(operation);
         mBufferManager.incrementNumCommandBufferCommits();
     }
     else
     {
         mCmdBuffer.wait(operation);
     }
 }
